<title>FINLAND: FINNISH 1996 EXPORTS THROUGH PORTS RISE.</title>
<headline>FINNISH 1996 EXPORTS THROUGH PORTS RISE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish 1996 exports through ports excluding transit cargo amounted to 30.85 million tonnes, up 0.22 million tonnes on 1995, the Board of Navigation said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a significant increase in exports of pulp, oil products and fertilisers, while exports of forest industry products (excluding pulp), metal products and chemicals fell clearly,&quot; the Board of Navigation said.</p>
<p>Imports through ports excluding transit cargo amounted to 35.23 million tonnes in 1996, down 0.55 million tonnes on 1995.  </p>
<p>In December, Finnish exports through ports including</p>
<p>transit cargo rose 3.7 percent year-on-year to 2.76 million</p>
<p>tonnes, but imports fell 0.7 percent year-on-year to 3.47</p>
<p>million tonnes, the Board of Navigation said.</p>
<p>It gave the following statistics for full-year 1996:</p>
<p>Cargo including transit cargo (million tonnes):</p>
<p>			  1996	   1995</p>
<p>  Imports	    36.94	  37.04</p>
<p>    own imports    35.23	  35.78</p>
<p>    transit	   1.71	   1.26</p>
<p>  Exports	    33.34	  34.12</p>
<p>    own exports    30.85	  30.63</p>
<p>    transit	   2.49	   3.49</p>
<p>  Total		70.28	  71.16</p>
<p>    own shipments  66.08	  66.41</p>
<p>    transit	   4.20	   4.75</p>
<p>Passenger traffic (millions of passengers):</p>
<p>			  1996	   1995</p>
<p>  Arrivals	    7.05	    6.98</p>
<p>  Departures	  7.01	    6.93</p>
<p>  Total		14.06	   13.91</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248</p>
</text>
